#: manual/semantics.md:1
msgid "Semantic design"
msgstr ""

#: manual/semantics.md:3
msgid "The operational semantics is defined by structured single-step reduction. Bounded normalizers and traces repeatedly invoke that interface."
msgstr ""

#: manual/semantics.md:6
msgid "NbE is an independent denotational implementation using lazy delayed terms, closures, neutral levels, and quote. It shares De Bruijn scope and binder primitives with the operational reducer and is checked for result agreement."
msgstr ""

#: manual/semantics.md:10
msgid "Named and De Bruijn syntax are both public. Conversion into De Bruijn removes alpha-renaming from the reduction kernel; conversion back selects deterministic fresh names."
msgstr ""

#: manual/semantics.md:14
msgid "Any custom AST that implements `BindingSyntax` can use generic substitution and rewrite traversal. Rewrite rules, domain evaluation, canonicalization, and fixed-point policies are defined by the downstream AST and are not fixed semantics of this module."
msgstr ""

#: manual/semantics.md:19
msgid "Expected failures at public boundaries are represented as structured data. `RuleName::new`, for example, returns `RuleNameError::Empty` for an empty name. Aborting `unsafe_*` constructors are reserved for callers that already establish the corresponding internal invariant."
msgstr ""
